(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \n",
 "Advanced Lesson 6\n\nAssignments\nReplacement Rules\n\nDr. Dale R. Doty\n\
University of Tulsa"
}], "Title"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Assignments  \"=\"  and  \":=\"", "Subtitle"]], \
"Section"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Remove", "[", "\"\<Global`*\>\"", " ", "]"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Immediate Assignment:", "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 " You can assign ANY result in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " to a symbol."
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
lhs = rhs evaluates rhs and assigns the result to be the value of lhs.
From then on, lhs is replaced by rhs whenever it appears.\
\>", "Item",
 GeneratedCell->False,
 CellAutoOverwrite->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900002167223997`*^9, 3.3900002236764*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"x1", "=", "3"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"x1", " ", "+", "x2"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"y1", " ", "=", " ", 
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"x1", " ", "+", "x2"}], ")"}], "2"]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["y1"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["x1", "2"], " ", "+", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{" ", "x2"}]]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "f1"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Note the immediate assignment \"=\" of  f1[...], and therefore immediate \
replacement of x1.

You can assign anything to a Mathematica symbol.  
For example, consider assigning the following plot to the Mathematica symbol \
\"plot1\":\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot1", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Plot", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox["x2"], ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x2", ",", "0", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["Examine the contents of the symbol \"plot1\":", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"InputForm", "[", "plot1", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389782387078*^9, 3.389782390237*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
You can now reference the Mathematica commands required to generate this \
graph at any time by evaluating:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389782432074*^9, 3.3897824456*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData["plot1"], "Input"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Assignments: Immediate Versus Delayed:", "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If the assignment uses the symbol \"=\", then ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " immediately searches for any values assigned to symbols appearing in the \
rhs and immediately replaces them with these values, then evaluates and \
simplifies the rhs and then replaces the lhs with the result, which is used \
every time thereafter. \n\nIf the assignment uses the symbol \": =\", then ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " will delay replacing assigned values to symbols appearing in the rhs until \
the lhs is actually used."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523113441250559*^9}],

Cell["\<\
 =
lhs = rhs evaluates rhs and assigns the result to be the value of lhs. 
From then on, lhs is replaced by rhs whenever it appears. \"
 :=
lhs := rhs assigns rhs to be the delayed value of lhs.
rhs is maintained in an unevaluated form.
When lhs appears, it is replaced by rhs, evaluated afresh each time.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900002433484*^9, 3.3900002837934*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\

As a first example, consider the Print[...] command.  You should understand \
that the Print[...] command is like a fire cracker -- once it has exploded \
(i.e. printed) the command has completely finished its task of printing and \
it no longer has content (i.e. is \"Null\" after it has printed).  Therefore, \
say that you want to print an expression several times and you would like to \
store the print command in a symbol for your convenience using either \
immediate or delayed assignment.  
If you use immediate assignment (i.e. \"=\") then the right hand side (i.e. \
the Print[...] command) will be evaluated now (i.e. printed now) with no \
remaining expression to be assigned to the symbol \"immediatePrint\".\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"immediatePrint", "  ", "=", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
  "Print", "[", "\"\<This is from the Print Command!\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Observe that the Print[...] command was evaluated.  So what remains to be \
assigned to the symbol \"immediatePrint\"? \nOn the other hand, if you delay \
the assignment (i.e. use \":=\") then the Print[...] command will ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " be evaluated now (i.e. it will not print now) and therefore the symbol \
\"delayedPrint\" will contain the full Print[...] command."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"delayedPrint", "  ", ":=", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
  "Print", "[", "\"\<This is from the Print Command!\>\"", 
   "]"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell["\<\
Observe that the Print[...] command was not evaluated.  
Next, evaluate both immediatePrint and delayedPrint and observe the results:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData["immediatePrint"], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

and
\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData["delayedPrint"], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Observe that immediatePrint did not produce printed output, while \
delayedPrint did.  
The following displays the contents of both symbols, which explains their \
respective behavior.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "immediatePrint"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "delayedPrint"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
It should now be clear that there are circumstances in which delayed \
assignment is preferred over immediate assignment and vice versa.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\

Next, consider the following example:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"random2", "=", 
  RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"random3", ":=", 
  RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Table", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"random2", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", "1", ",", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Table", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"random3", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", "1", ",", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note that in the first case the symbol \"random2\" has been immediately \
assigned (i.e. \"=\" ) a value which will be used for ",
 StyleBox["all",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " subsequent references to this symbol.  However in the second case, the \
symbol \"random3\" has been defined with a delayed evaluation (i.e. \":=\" ) \
which will result in a ",
 StyleBox["new",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " value corresponding to each use."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "random2"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "random3"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Most of the time, it is desirable to use delayed assignment (i.e. \":=\" ) \
when assigning a definition to a function.  This will prevent any previously \
assigned values from being used in the construction of the rhs of the \
function (and therefore being used forever). Delayed assignment will NOT use \
any previously assigned values for the rhs UNTIL you are ready to use that \
function along with the assigned values that you WANT for the rhs.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"z1", "=", "5"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
   RowBox[{"z1_", ",", "z2_"}], "]"}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["z1", "2"], " ", "+", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{" ", "z2"}]]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "f2"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Note the immediate assignment (i.e. \"=\" ) in the definition of:  f2[...].  \
Note the immediate replacement of z1 into the definition of:  f2[...].

Likewise:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f3", "[", 
   RowBox[{"z1_", ",", "z2_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["z1", "2"], " ", "+", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{" ", "z2"}]]}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "f3"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Note the delayed assignment (i.e. \":=\" ) in the definition of:  f3[...].  \
Note that no replacement of z1 was made into f3[...] when it was defined.

Therefore:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"f3", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
 Note that the value of z1 was replaced immediately in the function f2 but \
not in f3.\
\>", "Text"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Multiple Assignments:", "Subsection"],

Cell["\<\
Several assignments can be made with a single statement.  The assignments are \
made from right to left.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"x4", "=", 
  RowBox[{"y4", "=", "66"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["x4"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["y4"], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
 However, notice that the assignment MUST be from right to left.  Observe \
that the following command would assign a value of \"v4\" to the number 66, \
which results in an error.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
u4 = 66 = v4
Set::setraw : Cannot assign to raw object 66.
v4\
\>", "Program",
 GeneratedCell->False,
 CellAutoOverwrite->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900009187324*^9, 3.3900009189834003`*^9}, {
  3.390037741175*^9, 3.3900377495030003`*^9}}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Unassigning Values:", "Subsection"],

Cell["\<\
Once a symbol (or a function) has been assigned a value, then the way to \
clear a previous assignment is to use the Clear, ClearAll or Remove commands.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"x5", "=", "55"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f5", "[", "x_", "]"}], "=", 
  SqrtBox["x"]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"g5", "[", "x_", "]"}], ":=", 
  SqrtBox["x"]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", 
  RowBox[{"x5", ",", "f5", ",", "g5"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "x5"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "f5"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "g5"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
The Clear command clears the assignment to a symbol (or function), however if \
you have assigned any additional attributes to this symbol they will not be \
cleared.  Also, the name of the symbol will not be removed. 

For example, define the function  g5  without assigning additional attributes.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231136942685814`*^9, 3.5231136947521844`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"g5", "[", "x_", "]"}], ":=", 
  SqrtBox["x"]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell["Notice that the set of attributes for  g5  is empty:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Attributes", "[", "g5", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389782821092*^9, 3.3897828248190002`*^9}, {
  3.389782885653*^9, 3.389782896604*^9}}],

Cell["Next, assign the attribute of Listable to the function  g5:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"SetAttributes", " ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"g5", ",", " ", "Listable"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell["Note that it now has an attribute of Listable:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"??", 
  RowBox[{
  "g5", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "Global`g5", "\[IndentingNewLine]", GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Attributes", "[", "g5", "]"}], "=", 
       RowBox[{"{", "Listable", "}"}]}]},
     {" "},
     {GridBox[{
        {
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"g5", "[", "x_", "]"}], ":=", 
          SqrtBox["x"]}]}
       },
       BaselinePosition->{Baseline, {1, 1}},
       GridBoxAlignment->{
        "Columns" -> {{Left}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}},
          "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
       GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{
            Scaled[0.999]}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {{1.}}, 
         "RowsIndexed" -> {}}]}
    },
    BaselinePosition->{Baseline, {1, 1}},
    GridBoxAlignment->{
     "Columns" -> {{Left}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}, 
      "RowsIndexed" -> {}}]}]}]], "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900373247209997`*^9, 3.390037364388*^9}}],

Cell[" Next, clear the function:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "g5", "]"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell["\<\
 Observe that the assignment has been removed but not the attributes or the \
name.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
?? g5
   Global`g5
   Attributes[g5] = {Listable\
\>", "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.390037403969*^9, 3.390037436494*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
The ClearAll command performs the same function as the Clear command, however \
it also removes any attributes assigned to a symbol (but not the symbol's \
name).\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "g5", "]"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell["\<\
Observe that all assignments and attributes have been removed, but the symbol \
name \"Global`g5\" remains.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
?? g5
  Global`g5\
\>", "Program",
 GeneratedCell->False,
 CellAutoOverwrite->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39003746284*^9, 3.390037465722*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
 If you want to remove everything, including the symbol's name, then use the \
Remove command.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{"Remove", " ", "[", "g5", "]"}]}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell["\<\
?? g5
    Information::\"notfound\" : \"Symbol g5 not found.\" >>\
\>", "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900374864630003`*^9, 3.3900375390480003`*^9}}],

Cell["\<\

In Summary:
You have now learned that a symbol in Mathematica has three components:

\t I: \t Its name \t\t (removed by: Remove) 
 \t II: \t Its assigned values \t (removed by: Clear, ClearAll or Remove)
\t III:\t Its attributes\t \t (removed by: ClearAll or Remove)
\t \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox[" Important note:",
  FontSize->18],
 " The Remove command must be used to remove a name entered in context Global \
by accident when your intention is for the name to reference a different \
context (i.e. a name in a different package)."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->14,
 FontWeight->"Bold"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Replacement Rules   \"\[Rule]\"   And   \"\
\[RuleDelayed]\"", "Subtitle"]], "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Immediate Replacement Rules (\"\[Rule]\"):", "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The general form of an immediate replacement rule is:\n\n \t\texpression(  \
.... ",
 StyleBox["value1",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 " ......)  /.   ",
 StyleBox["value1",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 " \[Rule]  ",
 StyleBox["value2",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 "       \nyields:  \n \t\texpression(  .... ",
 StyleBox["value2",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 " ......)"
}], "Text"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "  Examples Using ",
 StyleBox["Explicit",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " Symbols:"
}], "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The following examples illustrate replacement rules using ",
 StyleBox["explicit",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " symbols or expressions, such as:  x, y, z, Sin[\[Alpha]], Cos[\[Beta]],  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "2"], " ", "+", "  ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "2"], " "}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "  etc.  \n\nConsider the following examples:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"x", " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}]}], "  ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "3"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], "  ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "3"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "z", "]"}], "  ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"z", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", "y"}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}], "  ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"{", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "3"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"y", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "4"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SuperscriptBox["x", "y"], "   ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"{", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"y", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"r", "*", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "2"], " ", "+", "  ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "2"], " ", "+", "  ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "2"]}], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   "1"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  FractionBox[
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Beta]", "]"}]}]], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Beta]", "]"}]}]], " ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], "\[Rule]", "a"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Beta]", "]"}], "\[Rule]", "b"}]}], 
   "}"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Observe that in each of the above examples, whenever the ",
 StyleBox["explicit",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " symbol or expression  ",
 StyleBox["lhs",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 "  was found in the main expression, the replacement rule  ",
 StyleBox["lhs",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 " \[Rule] ",
 StyleBox["rhs",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 "  causes it to be replaced by  ",
 StyleBox["rhs",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 "."
}], "Text"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "  Extended Example Using ",
 StyleBox["Explicit",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " Symbols:"
}], "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The purpose of the following example is to illustrate how natural \
replacement rules are in everyday mathematics.  Essentially, whenever you \
manipulate an expression algebraically you are replacing one part of the \
expression with something else.  This procedure can always be accomplished \
using replacement rules.\nConsider the following example.  Use trigonometric \
identities to simplify the following expression:\n\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    RowBox[{"8", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"8", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "4"], " "}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t\t"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start by replacing   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "4"], "  "}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " with the expression   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", "  ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ":"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   RowBox[{"8", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{"8", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "4"]}]}], " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "4"], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", "  ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Expand the above expression to allow for internal cancellation:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523114005786978*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Expand", "[", " ", 
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   RowBox[{"8", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{"8", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}]}], " ", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nNext, replace   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"], "  "}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " with the expression   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "x"}], "]"}], "2"], ")"}], "2"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523114008126993*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   RowBox[{"8", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}]}], "  ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}], "  ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "x"}], "]"}], "2"], ")"}], "2"]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nFinally, replace  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "x"}], "]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "  with the expression   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"4", " ", "x"}], "]"}]}], "2"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231140102330065`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "x"}], "]"}], "2"]}]}], "   ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "x"}], "]"}], "2"], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "x"}], "]"}]}], "2"]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

To check our answer, we will simplify the original expression:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231139138399887`*^9, 3.5231139144015923`*^9}, 
   3.523114012214219*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", " ", 
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   RowBox[{"8", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{"8", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "4"]}]}], " ", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231139052287335`*^9, 3.523113905790337*^9}}],

Cell["\<\

Although the above example illustrates how one typically makes mathematical \
substitutions, it is not very general.  To really increase the power of \
replacement rules one must combine pattern matching with replacement rules.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523114092461134*^9}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "  Examples Using ",
 StyleBox["Pattern Matching",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " :"
}], "Subsection"],

Cell["\<\
Consider the following examples which combine pattern matching and \
replacement rules together.

In the following two examples, the replacements match the pattern:  f [ a_ ]. \
 Remember that the pattern \"a_\" matches any single object specified by \
\"_\" and gives that object the local name  a.  The behavior of the local \
name  a  is similar to the behavior of the local name of a variable used to \
define a function.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], "  ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"f", "[", "a_", "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["a", "2"]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Here the replacement rule matches twice:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523113983962438*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"f", "[", "x1", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
    RowBox[{"f", "[", "x2", "]"}], "]"}]}], "  ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"f", "[", "a_", "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["a", "2"]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Apply a trigonometric identity in more general form:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523114018984663*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SqrtBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", "x"}], "]"}], "2"]], "  ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]_", "]"}], "2"], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "2"]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nNotice that in the above replacement rule, there is both an explicit part \
  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "...", "]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "  which must be ",
 StyleBox["matched precisely",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ", and a general pattern matching part   \[Theta]_   which will match ",
 StyleBox["any",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " single object and assign it the local name  \[Theta].\nHere the \
replacement rule matches three different patterns:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231140210906763`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", " ", "x"}], "]"}], "2"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"4", "\[Pi]", " ", "x"}], "]"}], "2"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"6", "\[Pi]", " ", "x"}], "]"}], "2"]}]], "  ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]_", "]"}], "2"], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "2"]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThis example requires two patterns (i.e. both  a_  and  n_ ) in the \
expression  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SqrtBox[
    SuperscriptBox["a_", "n_"]], TraditionalForm]]],
 "  to be matched before the replacement rule can be applied."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231140277987194`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SqrtBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "200"]], "   ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SuperscriptBox["a_", "n_"]], "  ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["a", 
    RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}]]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nNotice that in the above replacement rule, there is both an explicit part \
  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    SqrtBox[
     SuperscriptBox["...", "..."]],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "  which must be ",
 StyleBox["matched precisely",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ", and general pattern matching parts   a_  and   n_   which will match a \
pair of ",
 StyleBox["any",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " single objects and assign them the local names  a  and  n.\nHere the \
replacement rule matches four different patterns:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231140301231337`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "10"]], "  ", "+", "  ", 
   SqrtBox[
    SuperscriptBox["x", "200"]], "  ", "+", "  ", 
   SqrtBox[
    SuperscriptBox["y", "z"]], "  ", "+", "  ", 
   SqrtBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}]]]}], "   ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SuperscriptBox["a_", "n_"]], "  ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["a", 
    RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}]]}]}]], "Input"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Repeated Replacement Rules:", "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is possible to have the same rule repeatedly applied to an expression.  \
This will be required when the replacement rule modifies the ",
 StyleBox["full",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " expression.\n\nThe general form of a repeated replacement rule is:\n\n \t\t\
expression(  .... ",
 StyleBox["value1",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 "...",
 StyleBox["value1",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 "...",
 StyleBox["value1",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 " ....)   //.   ",
 StyleBox["value1",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 " \[Rule]  ",
 StyleBox["value2",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 "       \nyields:  \n \t\texpression(  .... ",
 StyleBox["value2",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 "...",
 StyleBox["value2",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 "...",
 StyleBox["value2",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]],
 "....)\n \t\t"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For example, assume that you wish to create a user defined function \
myLog[...] which behaves ",
 StyleBox["like",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " the logarithmic function  Log[...].   The first characteristic which you \
would want your function to have is to mimic the rule:  Log[ x y ]  \[Rule] \
Log[x] + Log[y].  Try this out on the following expression:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"myLog", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", "*", "b", "*", "c", "*", "d"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"myLog", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x_", "*", "y_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"myLog", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"myLog", "[", "y", "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Notice that the replacement rule was only used once, when you want it to be \
used two more times.
However, if repeated replacement is used:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523114068951783*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"myLog", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", "*", "b", "*", "c", "*", "d"}], "]"}], " ", "//.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"myLog", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x_", "*", "y_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"myLog", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"myLog", "[", "y", "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

The replacement rule will be applied all three times.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231140729142084`*^9}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
  Extended Example of Replacement Rules with Pattern Matching:\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3901935015810003`*^9, 3.390193517925*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The following example illustrates how replacement rules can be used to \
perform differential Calculus.  The idea is to create a replacement rule \
which will mimic the behavior of each differentiation rule that you learned \
in Calculus I.  \n\nWe will define a new function   ddx[ f[x] ]   which will \
mimic the behavior of the Calculus function   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", " ", 
      RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], " "}], 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]]],
 ".\nStart with the summation rule:\n\t\tCalculus:\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "x", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"d", " ", 
       RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], " "}], 
      RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " ", "+", " ", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"d", " ", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "x", "]"}]}], 
      RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " "}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\n\t\tYour Function:\tddx[ f[x] + g[x] ]  \[Rule]  ddx[ f[x] ] + ddx[ \
g[x] ]\n\t\t\nTest the summation rule:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["x", "5"], "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"]}], "  ", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
    RowBox[{"f_", "+", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], " ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThink ",
 StyleBox["carefully",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " why we ",
 StyleBox["had",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " to use the pattern   ddx[ f_ + g_ ]    rather than   ddx[ f[x_] + g[x_] ].\
\n\nNext, attempt to apply our summation rule to a much more complicated \
formula:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.523114134784205*^9, 3.5231141473266854`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "5"], "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], " ", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
    RowBox[{"f_", "+", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], " ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Observe that only one replacement was made.  

Therefore use repeated replacement:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231141501659036`*^9, 3.5231141534887247`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "5"], "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], " ", "]"}], " ", "//.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
    RowBox[{"f_", "+", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], " ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nObserve that the above differentiation rule was applied four times.\n\n\
Next, add the product rule:\n\t\tCalculus:\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "*", " ", 
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "x", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], "d", " ", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "x", "]"}], " "}], 
       RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"d", " ", 
        RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}]}], 
       RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "x", "]"}], " "}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\n\t\tYour Function:\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "*", " ", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "]"}], "  ", "\[Rule]", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
        RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}]}],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "\n\t\t\nTest the product rule:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231141568115463`*^9, 3.52311415893316*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "*", 
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "]"}], " ", "//.", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
    RowBox[{"f_", "*", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f", "*", 
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}], " ", "+", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], "*", "g"}]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Apply both the summation rule and the product rule to the original equation:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231141649859986`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "5"], "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], " ", "]"}], " ", "//.", " ", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"f_", "+", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], " ", "+", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"f_", "*", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f", "*", 
       RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}], " ", "+", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], "*", "g"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nObserve that the product rule was applied twice.\n\nNext, add the power \
rule:\n\t\tCalculus:\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], "n"], " ", ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"n", "  ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], 
      RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]], 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"d", " ", 
       RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], " "}], 
      RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " "}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n",
 "\n\t\tYour Function:\tddx[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], "n"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]  \[Rule]  n ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], 
    RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ddx[ f[x] ]\n\t\t\nTest the power rule:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231141723960457`*^9, 3.5231141745176597`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"], " ", "]"}], " ", "//.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
    SuperscriptBox["f_", 
     RowBox[{" ", "n_"}]], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   RowBox[{"n", "*", 
    SuperscriptBox["f", 
     RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]], " ", 
    RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", "f", " ", "]"}]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Apply the summation rule, the product rule and the power rule to the original \
equation:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231141780900826`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "5"], "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], " ", "]"}], " ", "//.", " ", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"f_", "+", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], " ", "+", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"f_", "*", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f", "*", 
       RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}], " ", "+", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], "*", "g"}]}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      SuperscriptBox["f_", 
       RowBox[{" ", "n_"}]], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"n", "*", 
      SuperscriptBox["f", 
       RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", "f", " ", "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nObserve that the power rule was applied twice.\n\nFinally, add the \
remaining rules required to complete the differentiation:\n\t\tCalculus:\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", " ", "x", " ", ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "1", " "}], 
   TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\t\t\t\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}], " "}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\t\t\t\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "x"}]], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sec", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"], " "}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n",
 "\n\t\tYour Function:\tddx[ x ]  \[Rule]  1 \n\t\t\t\t\tddx[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]  \[Rule]  Cos[ x ] \n\t\t\t\t\tddx[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " ]  \[Rule]  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"Sec", "[", " ", "x", " ", "]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " \n\t\t\nTest the new rules:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.523114185000927*^9, 3.52311418709134*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "]"}], " ", "//.", " ", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"f_", "+", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], " ", "+", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"Sec", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Apply all of the above rules to the original equation:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523114209649085*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "5"], "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], " ", "]"}], " ", "//.", " ", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"f_", "+", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], " ", "+", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"f_", "*", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f", "*", 
       RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "g", "]"}]}], " ", "+", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "f", "]"}], "*", "g"}]}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      SuperscriptBox["f_", 
       RowBox[{" ", "n_"}]], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"n", "*", 
      SuperscriptBox["f", 
       RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]], " ", 
      RowBox[{"ddx", "[", " ", "f", " ", "]"}]}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x", "]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ddx", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"Sec", "[", "x", "]"}], "2"]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nObserve that all require differentiation has been completed.\n\nTo check \
our answer, use ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "'s internal differentiation:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.523114216481929*^9, 3.523114219508348*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], " ", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "5"], "+", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "3"], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "*", 
     RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Our differentiation accomplished by pattern matching and replacement rules \
works!  To make the above code both complete and bulletproof requires a \
little more effort.  However, the procedure is essentially the same.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.38978364213*^9, 3.389783643413*^9}, 
   3.523114223236772*^9}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Replacement Rules As Output From A Mathematica Command:", "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 " A number of different ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " commands yield replacement rules as their output:\n\t\tSolve[...]\n\t\t\
DSolve[...]\n\t\tetc.\n As an example, consider solving two simultaneous \
equations:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"theRoots", " ", "=", " ", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], " ", "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["y", "2"]}], " ", "==", "6"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"y", "==", 
       SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389783667948*^9, 3.389783693699*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"theRoots", "//", " ", "TableForm"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

In order to check our solutions, we can use the replacement rules to \
substitute into the two equations (note that when the logical operator = = is \
satisfied, we get True).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231142855435715`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "+", 
       SuperscriptBox["y", "2"]}], "\[Equal]", "6"}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"y", "\[Equal]", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], "/.", "\[InvisibleSpace]", "theRoots"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3897837209119997`*^9, 3.389783770475*^9}}],

Cell["\<\

As a second example, assume that you need to substitute the solutions found \
above into the exponent of an exponential function using the replacement \
rules:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231142807855406`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
    RowBox[{" ", 
     RowBox[{"x", " ", "+", " ", "y"}]}]], "  ", "/.", " ", "theRoots"}], 
  "        ", "//", "TableForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.389783793572*^9}],

Cell["\<\

As a third example, consider task of minimizing a function.  The procedure \
used will be to:

\t I: \t Differentiate and set the derivative equal to 0 and solve for  x
\t II: \t Check the sign of the second derivative to make sure it is a local \
minimum
\t \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231142892875957`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f", "[", "x_", "]"}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{"4", " ", "x"}], " ", "+", " ", "5"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", "4"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", "6"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Solve", "[", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "'"}], "[", "x", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], " ", ",", 
   " ", "x"}], " ", "]"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Find the value of the function at the minimum point:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231142988348565`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], "  ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"x", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Check that this value corresponds to a critical point:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523114301798876*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"f", "'"}], "[", "x", "]"}], "  ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"x", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Check the sign of the second derivative:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231143064789057`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f", "'"}], "'"}], "[", "x", "]"}], "  ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"x", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}]], "Input"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
  Delayed Replacement Rules (\"\[RuleDelayed]\") vs. Immediate Replacement \
Rules (\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]\[Rule]\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]):\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.523114432527714*^9, 3.523114454586255*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Immediate replacement:    value1 \[Rule] value2",
  FontSize->14,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\nThe full form for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "\[Rule]", "b"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " is:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.523114471730765*^9, 3.523114497595731*^9}, {
   3.523114793576428*^9, 3.5231147986308603`*^9}, 3.5231151782748938`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", "\[Rule]", "b"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231143826853943`*^9, 3.5231143974274883`*^9}}],

Cell["\<\

With attributes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.523114506035385*^9, 3.5231145441776295`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Attributes", "[", "Rule", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231144022947197`*^9, 3.523114411217977*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nImmediate replacement rules do NOT hold their arguments:    \n\n\t\
expression(  .... value1 ......)  /. value1 \[Rule]  value2 ,    \n\t\nthen:  \
 \n\n\tvalue1 \[Rule]  value2   \n\t\n",
 StyleBox["both",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " value1 and value2 are evaluated first, and then the replacement is made \
second.  The consequence of this is that all replacements will have the same ",
 StyleBox["evaluated",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " quantity.  Sometimes this is not desired, i.e. when the replaced quantity \
should be evaluated AFTER the replacement has been invoked. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.389783876146*^9, {3.523114542867221*^9, 3.5231146415378532`*^9}, 
   3.523114788896398*^9, {3.5231148284114513`*^9, 3.523114851905202*^9}, {
   3.5231150754546347`*^9, 3.5231151243765483`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Delayed replacement:       value1 \[RuleDelayed] value2",
  FontSize->14,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\nThe full form for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "\[RuleDelayed]", "b"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " is:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.523114471730765*^9, 3.523114497595731*^9}, {
   3.523114699663826*^9, 3.523114699663826*^9}, {3.5231148445107546`*^9, 
   3.5231148469755707`*^9}, 3.5231151719724536`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{"a", "\[RuleDelayed]", "b"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231143826853943`*^9, 3.5231143974274883`*^9}, 
   3.523114714171919*^9}],

Cell["\<\

With attributes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.523114506035385*^9, 3.5231145441776295`*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Attributes", "[", "RuleDelayed", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231144022947197`*^9, 3.523114411217977*^9}, 
   3.5231147267455997`*^9}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nDelayed replacement rules ",
 StyleBox["DO",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " hold their ",
 StyleBox["second",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " argument:    \n\n\texpression(  .... value1 ......)  /. value1 \
\[RuleDelayed]  value2 ,    \n\t\nthen:   \n\n\tvalue1 \[RuleDelayed]  value2 \
  \n\t\nvalue1 is evaluated first but ",
 StyleBox["NOT",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " value2, and then the replacement is made.  The consequence of this is that \
all replacements will have the same ",
 StyleBox["un",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "evaluated quantity value2.  Sometimes this is not desired, i.e. when the \
replaced quantity should be evaluated BEFORE the replacement has been \
invoked. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.389783876146*^9, {3.523114542867221*^9, 3.5231146415378532`*^9}, 
   3.523114788896398*^9, {3.5231148284114513`*^9, 3.5231149384077563`*^9}, {
   3.5231149756139946`*^9, 3.5231150523664865`*^9}, {3.523115250518957*^9, 
   3.5231152526249704`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Delayed (\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]\[RuleDelayed]\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) vs. Immediate (\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]\[Rule]\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]):",
 FontSize->14,
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231153182233915`*^9, 3.5231153534016166`*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["lhs \[Rule] rhs   represents a rule that transforms lhs to rhs.", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900003128073997`*^9, 3.3900003435053997`*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\
lhs \[RuleDelayed] rhs   represents a rule that transforms lhs to rhs, \
evaluating rhs only when the rule is used.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3900003154564*^9, 3.3900003463543997`*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\

In the immediate replacement rule that follows, Random [ ] was evaluated and \
a table with the same five elements was created.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3897838862460003`*^9, 3.389783892196*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", "1", ",", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "/.", 
  "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
  RowBox[{"x", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", "]"}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

However, using delayed replacement, Random [ ] was delayed in its evaluation \
(i.e. five copies of the function  Random [ ] were put into a table) and a \
table with five different elements was created when the function Random [ ] \
was evaluated five separate times.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231153925890675`*^9, 3.52311539301027*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", "1", ",", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "/.", 
  "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
  RowBox[{"x", "\[RuleDelayed]", 
   RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", "]"}]}]}]], "Input"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Assigning The Results Of A Replacement Rule:", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3901935221619997`*^9}],

Cell["\<\
It is important to understand that a replacement rule used to modify an \
expression does not reassign the value of that expression to anything else.  \
Consider the following example:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["Note that x does not have an assigned value:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "x"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Next, replace x:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3897840731540003`*^9, 3.3897840960629997`*^9}, 
   3.5231154387029634`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"x", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "\"\<NewValue\>\""}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nNote that x does not have an ",
 StyleBox["assigned",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " value:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231154403877745`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "x"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

However, if the replacement rule is used AND the result assigned to \"x\", \
then the replaced value of \"x\" will be assigned to \"x\".\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.389784127885*^9, 3.5231154439601974`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"x", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"x", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "\"\<NewValue\>\""}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "x"}]], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\n Warning, it is usually better to make the assignment to a ",
 StyleBox["new",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " symbol name."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.523115450231437*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"xNew", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"x", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "\"\<NextNewValue\>\""}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["x"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["xNew"], "Input"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Example:", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.390193525733*^9}],

Cell["\<\
Often you want to use the solution (i.e. represented as a replacement rule) \
arising from something like Solve[...] and define a function:
\t\tf[x_] = ... solution ...
\t\t
The following procedure illustrates how this is done:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3897842659049997`*^9, 3.3897842789119997`*^9}, {
   3.3897843558570004`*^9, 3.389784361719*^9}, 3.523115474754794*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", 
  RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "f"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly"],

Cell["Solve the following algebraic equation for y:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389784386006*^9, 3.389784388252*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRule", " ", "=", 
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "*", "y"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", "y"}]}], " ", "\[Equal]", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}], ",", "y"}], "]"}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Observe that the solution is given as a replacement rule.

The proper procedure to define a function using this replacement rule is as \
follows:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.523115485908866*^9, 3.523115491930505*^9}}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f", "[", "x_", "]"}], "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"y", " ", "/.", " ", 
   RowBox[{"y", "\[Rule]", 
    FractionBox[
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], 
     RowBox[{"4", "+", "x"}]]}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Verify that the function definition is as expected:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.52311549441092*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "f"}]], "Input"],

Cell["\<\

Finally, plot the function and its first two derivatives:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231155073746033`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f", "'"}], "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f", "''"}], "[", "x", "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], 
   ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.38978442165*^9, 3.389784436821*^9}}]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
  Controlling The Range Of Application For A Replacement Rule:\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.389784450758*^9, 3.390193528538*^9}],

Cell["\<\
As an expression becomes more complicated, it may be necessary to limit the \
range of application of a replacement rule.  This can easily be accomplished \
using parentheses.  

As an example consider the following:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.389784558602*^9, 3.389784558943*^9}, 
   3.5231155361411877`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Log", "[", "z", "]"}], "+", 
   RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "z", "]"}], "+", 
   RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "z", "]"}]}], "   ", "/.", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"z", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["\[Pi]", "180"], "\[Theta]"}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Log", "[", "z", "]"}], "+", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "z", "]"}], "+", 
     RowBox[{"Tan", "[", "z", "]"}]}], "   ", "/.", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"z", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["\[Pi]", "180"], "\[Theta]"}]}]}], ")"}]}]], "Input"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Assignments Versus Replacement Rules:", "Subsection"],

Cell["\<\
Assignments assign a value to a symbol (or replace the previously made \
assignment with the new assignment). 

Replacement rules make a replacement within an expression to yield a new \
expression as output.  However, the original expression remains unchanged and \
no assignments are made.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.5231155662805815`*^9}],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"y", "=", "\"\<OriginalAssignmentToY\>\""}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "y"}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"yAssigned", "=", 
  RowBox[{"y", " ", "/.", " ", 
   RowBox[{"y", " ", "\[Rule]", "\"\<ReplacementValueForY\>\""}]}]}]], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["y"], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData["yAssigned"], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nNote that the value of the symbol \"y\" remains unchanged after the \
replacement rule has been used.  However, the  \"ReplacementValueForY\"  has \
now been assigned to \"yAssigned\".\n\nThus, if you want to use a replacement \
rule ",
 StyleBox["and",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " have the original expression replaced with the resulting expression, then \
it ",
 StyleBox["must",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " be explicitly assigned to some symbol."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5231155892751284`*^9, 3.523115606825241*^9}}]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox[" Exercises:", "Title"],
 "  Advanced Lesson 6 "
}], "Section"],

Cell["\<\
Your Name:

Your Math Class:\
\>", "Program",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.390368232619*^9, 3.3903682391219997`*^9}, {
   3.390368866851*^9, 3.390368908736*^9}, {3.3903690435030003`*^9, 
   3.390369082222*^9}, 3.3903880065649595`*^9},
 FontSize->16,
 FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Note: Some of the following exercises are expressed in every day \
mathematical notation rather than proper ", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["Mathematica", "Subsubsection",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 StyleBox[" notation.  You ", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["MUST", "Subsubsection",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 StyleBox[" convert every day notation into ", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["Mathematica", "Subsubsection",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 StyleBox[" notation for your code to work properly.  For example:\n\n\t\
Equations ", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["must", "Subsubsection",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 StyleBox[" be changed from  \"=\"  to  \"==\"  to work correctly (i.e. ", 
  "Subsubsection"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "\[Equal]", 
     RowBox[{"2", "x"}]}], "Subsubsection"], TraditionalForm]]],
 StyleBox["  not  ", "Subsubsection"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "=", 
     RowBox[{"2", "x"}]}], "Subsubsection"], TraditionalForm]]],
 StyleBox["  ).  \n\tFunctions ", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["must", "Subsubsection",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 StyleBox[" be expressed as  f[x]  and  not  f(x)  to work correctly.  \n\t\
Functions ", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["must", "Subsubsection",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 StyleBox[" be defined using  \"_\"  to work correctly (i.e.  ", 
  "Subsubsection"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "[", "x_", "]"}], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", 
       SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}], "+", "1"}]}], "Subsubsection"], 
   TraditionalForm]]],
 StyleBox["  and not  ", "Subsubsection"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "[", "x", "]"}], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", 
       SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}], "+", "1"}]}], "Subsubsection"], 
   TraditionalForm]]],
 StyleBox[").\n\t", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["Mathematica", "Subsubsection",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 StyleBox[" functions ", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["must", "Subsubsection",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 StyleBox[" start with a capital (i.e.  Sin[x]  not  sin[x]).\n\t", 
  "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["Your", "Subsubsection",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 StyleBox[" functions should start with a lower case letter (i.e.  f[x]  not  \
F[x]).\n\tSpecial symbols ", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["must", "Subsubsection",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 StyleBox[" be entered correctly (i.e.  ", "Subsubsection"],
 StyleBox["\[ExponentialE]", "Subsection"],
 StyleBox["  from the palette and not  e ).\n\t\nThese exercises begin your \
training in making this conversion automatically.\n", "Subsubsection"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39064873246*^9, 3.390649069177*^9}, {3.390649104818*^9, 
   3.390649156885*^9}, {3.390649215119*^9, 3.39064939362*^9}, {
   3.390649427467*^9, 3.390649437834*^9}, {3.3906856676331425`*^9, 
   3.3906858924611425`*^9}, {3.3906859679691424`*^9, 3.390686080823142*^9}, {
   3.390686138196142*^9, 3.390686244913142*^9}, 3.390686344335142*^9, {
   3.3906897169261427`*^9, 3.3906898397271423`*^9}, {3.3906898702421427`*^9, 
   3.3906898773081427`*^9}, {3.3906929183261423`*^9, 3.3906929191781425`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Remember to clear all variables that you will use below:  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "          ", "...", "             ", "]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3906923197301426`*^9, 3.3906923812721424`*^9}, {
  3.3906924809361424`*^9, 3.3906924908791423`*^9}, {3.3906927825761423`*^9, 
  3.3906927911761427`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1: Explain why the following code gives unexpected results.\n\tx = 2\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
    RowBox[{
     FormBox[
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"],
      TraditionalForm], 
     RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "x"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3903885877929597`*^9, 3.39038870608596*^9}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "2: Explain why the following code gives unexpected results.\n\tx := 2\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
    RowBox[{
     FormBox[
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"],
      TraditionalForm], 
     RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "x"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.39038859192196*^9, 3.3903887096759596`*^9}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "3: Explain why the following code gives unexpected results.\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"x", "=", "2"}], ";"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f1", "[", "x_", "]"}], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}], ";"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f2", "[", "x_", "]"}], ":=", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}], ";"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f1", "[", "z", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"f2", "[", "z", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"z", ",", "0", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", "0.01", "]"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ";"}]}],
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39038867141996*^9, 3.39038867223396*^9}, {
  3.39038935257796*^9, 3.39038936334296*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "4: Explain why the following code gives unexpected results.\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[{
  RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "  ", "/.", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "y"}]}]}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
     RowBox[{
      FormBox[
       SuperscriptBox["x", "2"],
       TraditionalForm], 
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "y"}]}]}],
    TraditionalForm], " "}]}],
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "5: Explain the results of the following code:\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[{
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "z"}], "]"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"], "\n", 
  RowBox[{" ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"x", "=", 
     RowBox[{"x", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "y"}]}]}],
    FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "\n", 
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
      RowBox[{
       FormBox[
        SuperscriptBox["x", "2"],
        TraditionalForm], 
       RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "y"}]}]}],
     TraditionalForm], " "}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]}]]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "6: Explain the results of the following code:\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[{
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "z"}], "]"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"], "\n", 
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{"x", "=", 
     RowBox[{"z", "  ", "/.", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"x", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "y"}]}]}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"], "\n", 
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
      RowBox[{
       FormBox[
        SuperscriptBox["x", "2"],
        TraditionalForm], 
       RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "y"}]}]}],
     TraditionalForm], " "}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]}]]
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
7: Explain why the following code does NOT yield:  Log[2 \[Pi] y]
\tClear [x,y]
\tSin[x]  /. {Sin[x] \[Rule] Log[x], x \[Rule] 2\[Pi] y}
How would you modify the replacement rule to yield the desired result?\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39038880315896*^9, 3.39038880315996*^9}}],

Cell["\<\
8: Explain how the following code works:
Clear [f,x,y,z]
\tf[x_] :=  x   /.  {y \[Rule] Cos[y],  z \[Rule] Sin[z]}
\tf[x]
\tf[x + y + z]\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
9: Explain the purpose of the replacement rules:  Frame \[Rule] False,  Frame \
\[Rule] True
\tClear [x]
\tPlot[Sin[x],{x,0,2\[Pi]}, Frame \[Rule] False]
\tPlot[Sin[x],{x,0,2\[Pi]}, Frame \[Rule] True]\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
10: Explain how the following code works:
\tClear [x,plot1,plot2]
\tplot1 = Plot[Sin[x], {x,0,2\[Pi]}, Frame \[Rule] True]
\t?plot1
\tplot2 = plot1  /.  (Frame\[Rule]{{True,True},{True,True}})  \[Rule]  (Frame \
\[Rule]{{False,True},{False,True}})
\t?plot2
\tShow[plot2]\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39038899765596*^9, 3.39038900699396*^9}, 
   3.6827906671779327`*^9, {3.6828580810652685`*^9, 3.6828581029832687`*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "11:   Part 1:   Solve the ODE:  y''[t] + y[t] = 0   to get a replacement \
rule for  y[t]  using  DSolve.\nPart 2:   Use a list of replacement rules to \
replace C[1] with  4  and C[2] with  7  in the replacement rule for y[t].\n\
Part 3:   Use the solution replacement rule and substitute back into the ODE \
to check the solution   (You MUST use a procedure ",
 StyleBox["similar",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " to the one I used above when I used the Solve command, however this \
example is harder than the one above).\nHint: How does  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "t"}]], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"y", "[", "t", "]"}], "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"f", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " evaluate?\nPart 4:   Use replacement rules to extract the solution  y[t]  \
from its replacement rule generated in Part 2 and use this to plot the \
solution for  0 \[LessEqual] t \[LessEqual] 2\[Pi]."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3903891510319595`*^9, 3.39038925853496*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Print",
  FontSize->14,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox[" your homework exercises",
  FontSize->14],
 ".\n",
 StyleBox["But do ",
  FontSize->14,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 StyleBox["NOT",
  FontSize->18,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 StyleBox[" print the above lesson along with the exercises!",
  FontSize->14,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]
}], "Text",
